Let me check if there's a way to trigger a more severe OOB read. Let me look at the `is_codefence` function one more time:

```c
c = data[i];
if (i + 2 >= size || !(c=='~' || c=='`'))
    return 0;

/* the fence must be that same character */
while (++i < size && data[i] == c)
